{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794230942,"nonce":"1pglIjqnietKK7Ipd2bfzbBZaD4=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-493a53c-integration` (0bed642..36e9608).\n\n**Changes**\n- src/keymap.rs: new. Pure `resolve(key, mods, ctx) -\u003e Option\u003cAction\u003e` over one binding table. Also `hint()` and `help_rows()`, which render that table per platform (⌘K or Ctrl+K). Unit tests included.\n- src/ui/shortcuts.rs: new help overlay, using the `done::overlay` stack and scrim pattern. Lists every binding by group.\n- src/main.rs: registers `mod keymap`.\n- src/app.rs: new `Message::{KeyPressed, FocusSearch, OpenCursor, ToggleHelp}`. New `cursor` and `help` state. The subscription now forwards all key presses, and `update` resolves them with the app context. j/k/↓/↑ move the cursor, and an open detail pane follows it. Enter opens, `x` closes or reopens, and Esc closes help first, then detail. Added app-level tests.\n- src/ui/screen.rs: the Search pill sends `FocusSearch`. The search `text_input` and the list `scrollable` got Ids, and Enter in the search box submits. Row highlight now follows the cursor. A keyboard-shortcuts pill was added to the top bar. Tooltip hints now show on the toggle-sidebar, theme, search, sidebar-nav and close/reopen controls.\n- src/ui/components.rs: added `icon_pill_hint` and `icon_square_button_hint`. The old functions delegate to them.\n- src/ui/tooltip.rs: added `shortcut_maybe`.\n- src/ui/mod.rs: registers `shortcuts`.\n\n**Gates:** tests ok · clippy ok · fmt ok\n**Review:** 3 findings — 3 auto, 0 by hand, 0 deferred\n\n**Decisions**\n- `keymap.rs` lives in the binary crate, not the lib, because `Section` is defined in `main.rs`.\n- `event::listen_with` takes a plain `fn` and cannot read app state. The subscription therefore emits `Message::KeyPressed { key, modifiers, typing }`, where `typing` means the event was already captured. `update` builds the `Context` and resolves the key. Cmd chords fire even while typing. Single-key bindings need `typing == false` and the Issues section. While help is open, only Help and Esc resolve.\n- For plain presses the shifted key is used, so `?` resolves. For command chords the unshifted key is used, so Cmd+Shift+L is `l`. Letter matching ignores case.\n- A new keyboard cursor (`App.cursor`) separates \"selected\" from \"detail open\". Clicking a row also sets it. Enter in the search box submits `OpenCursor`, which opens the first filtered row.\n- The list scroll follows the cursor with `snap_to(i/(n-1))`, which keeps a uniform-height row in view without measuring layout. `shown` grows when the cursor moves past the loaded page, and when a filter change would hide the cursor row.\n- Review fixes: `OpenCursor` now flushes the pending search and clears the cursor before opening the first result. `apply_filter` keeps the cursor row visible. A misplaced doc comment on `open_detail` was restored.\n- Not run: no live GUI check of focus-on-Cmd+K. Reading iced_winit confirms the view is rebuilt before widget operations run.","files":null}]}